    "created_at": "2018-03-20T06:56:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-20T06:56:20Z",
    "body": "In Chrome, when I navigate to `http://example.com/`, open the console, `document.open()`, `document.write(\"test\")`, `document.close()`, `history.back()`, I end up on `chrome://newtab`. That means it does effectively replace the current entry, no?\r\n\r\nThat is, history is not meddled with at all.\r\n\r\nAnd I think the only reason to support history of sorts here is to have Firefox's infrastructure (by making it create a new global), which means this is probably a soft duplicate of #1698.",
