    "updated_at": "2018-03-21T09:04:08Z",
    "body": "Yeah, because Firefox has a fundamentally different architecture.\r\n\r\nLast I talked to bz about this he seemed somewhat open to adopting the architecture of other browsers for `document.open()`, provided it had sufficient tests and their model was actually clear. Given the things we're discovering here their model might not be all that complex.",
